# Route Loading (`loading.tsx`)

Use Next.js `loading.tsx` + shared loader components for **segment suspense** while server content loads.

## Prefer skeletons for feature routes

Panel **feature** routes (lists, details, calendars, forms) should use **layout-shaped skeletons** from `@/components/loaders/skeletons` — see `.cursor/rules/loaders-skeletons.mdc`. Do not add a new centered “Loading page…” spinner when a `Panel*PageSkeleton` fits.

## Components

| Component | Path | Use in |
|-----------|------|--------|
| `RouteLoading` | `@/components/loaders/route-loading` | Auth/root full-page; panel **root** `loading.tsx` only |
| Skeleton templates | `@/components/loaders/skeletons` | Manager (and other) feature `loading.tsx` |
| `FullPageLoader` | `@/components/loaders/full-page-loader` | Full viewport waits outside panel content |

## Variants

```tsx
// Root or auth — full viewport
export default function Loading() {
  return <RouteLoading variant="full-page" label="Loading…" />;
}

// Panel root only (e.g. app/(panels)/manager/loading.tsx) — until a root skeleton exists
export default function PanelRootLoading() {
  return <RouteLoading variant="panel" label="Loading page…" />;
}

// Feature route — skeleton template
import { PanelListPageSkeleton } from "@/components/loaders/skeletons";

export default function Loading() {
  return <PanelListPageSkeleton />;
}
```

## When

- Add `loading.tsx` next to `page.tsx` when the page has async server work and should show a fallback.
- **Feature panel routes:** `Panel*PageSkeleton` templates.
- **Panel roots** (`admin` / `manager` / `teacher` / … `loading.tsx`): `RouteLoading variant="panel"` is acceptable.
- **Public/auth/root:** `variant="full-page"`.

## Do not

- Put business logic in `loading.tsx`.
- Use route loading for button/action pending states — use `InlineSpinner` instead.
- Add a new panel center spinner when a skeleton template fits.
- Import `PanelRouteLoading` for new feature fallbacks — prefer skeletons.
